sentences.l:
But you now drink, sitting, the fire-faced wine,
until the warm baths fine-plaited Hecamede
heats and washes off the bloody gore;

So saying, a shield he took, wrought, his own son’s,
lying in the hut of Thrasymedes, horse-taming,
with bronze gleaming all over;

and no longer could you tell, however much you were spying,
from which side the Achaeans, stirred up, are thrown into confusion,
so mixed together they are killed, and the cry reaches heaven.

and high on anchor-stones let us moor, until there comes
the immortal night, if even so they hold back from the war,
the Trojans;
